WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:07.400
The demon inside the hero. It’s a an anime&nbsp;
trope as old as time. Naruto and the nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:14.480
tails. Asta in Black clover. Ichigo in Bleach.&nbsp;
Inuyasha. Chainsawman. The list goes on and on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:20.400
and if you’ve watched any anime, like ever,&nbsp;
you will know that the main character always&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:27.640
has to face his inner demon, overcome it and then&nbsp;
grow stronger. You know, it’s a metaphor. So it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.880
actually quite refreshing, that Jujutsu Kaisen&nbsp;
took this anime trope, like so many others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:40.160
and flipped it completely on its head, as Itadori&nbsp;
Yuji is just crushed over and over again by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:46.920
far stronger and far smarter Sukuna. But…what&nbsp;
if Yuji was more like the rest of the Shonen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:53.600
Protagonist and could actually learn to control&nbsp;
Sukuna and make use of his insane powers?

00:00:54.120 --> 00:01:01.080
This one change would make the entire story&nbsp;
of Jujutsu Kaisen completely different. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:06.440
normal - but super strong - high school student&nbsp;
Yuji Itadori finds himself face to face with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:13.320
monstrous curse terrorizing his friends, he makes&nbsp;
a split-second decision that changes his life. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:19.880
eats a Special Grade Cursed Object: AKA one of the&nbsp;
twenty fingers of Sukuna. And as Gojo reminds us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:25.360
this isn’t counting toes - Sukuna has four&nbsp;
arms because he’s just built different.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:31.720
Normally, this would kill him instantly, but&nbsp;
Yuji is a super special shonen protagonist,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:35.960
so instead he emerges as a&nbsp;
suitable vessel for Sukuna.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:42.080
The thing is, Yuji isn’t able to access&nbsp;
any of Sukuna’s insane powers - he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.480
just take back control of his body&nbsp;
and suppress Sukuna inside of him.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:51.520
But what would it be like if instead of just&nbsp;
being able to take back control of his body,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.040
Yuji could actually just&nbsp;
access Sukuna’s insane power?

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.640
First off, Satoru Gojo would be a LOT more&nbsp;
suspicious of the whole situation. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:07.800
normal story, he fought with Sukuna for&nbsp;
ten seconds as a test to see if Yuji could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:14.680
take back control at will. But if normal Yuji was&nbsp;
ALSO as strong as Sukuna without him taking over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:19.280
he’d probably be more likely to think&nbsp;
Sukuna was just acting with his best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.440
Yuji impression to trick them into thinking he&nbsp;
was suppressed. Yuji would let the slashes fly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:30.160
giving Gojo about a million cuts that he’d&nbsp;
have to heal with Reverse Cursed Technique.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:36.720
Gojo would probably ask Yuji a series of questions&nbsp;
that only the real Yuji would know. He’d ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.360
stuff like “what’s your birth date?”, “What’s&nbsp;
your mother’s maiden name?” (it’s Kenjaku),&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.960
“What’s the name of the street you grew up on?”&nbsp;
Then, of course, Megumi would yell at his sensei&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:51.840
because neither of them would have any idea at&nbsp;
all what the answers to those questions were.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:59.280
The higher-ups, especially, would want Yuji dead,&nbsp;
just like they did in the normal story. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:05.960
the only thing more dangerous than a resurrected&nbsp;
ancient curse user is a teenager with unlimited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.960 --> 00:03:10.960
power. However, after Gojo was fully&nbsp;
satisfied that it was Yuji in control,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.400
he would still vouch for him and convince the&nbsp;
higher-ups. After all, he was Gojo, and he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:21.160
could simply stop Yuji if he went rogue since he&nbsp;
only had one finger’s worth of power at the time.

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:26.640
Of course, shortly after Yuji’s power level&nbsp;
would grow to two fingers as Gojo would give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:33.760
him another one that Jujutsu High had on hand as&nbsp;
a means of testing his ability as a vessel. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:40.160
each finger that Sukuna regains, his total&nbsp;
power grows. However, this doesn’t actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.000
affect Yuji’s base power. He still needs to&nbsp;
work on developing his own strength because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:51.440
he’s unable to access Sukuna’s well of power.&nbsp;
In this scenario, though, all of that finger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:58.080
power may as well be Yuji’s because he can use it&nbsp;
all without having to give up control to Sukuna.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:04.160
Now let’s flash forward to Yuji’s next big moment.&nbsp;
For a lot of fans, the point where they realized&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:10.600
that Jujutsu Kaisen was not their standard series&nbsp;
was when the main character nearly literally died&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:17.000
in just the sixth episode. But in this timeline,&nbsp;
with Yuji getting access to Sukuna’s power without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:21.920
him totally losing control, things would go down&nbsp;
very differently when the Special Grade Cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:28.000
Spirit showed up, spawning from the Cursed&nbsp;
Womb. This Cursed Womb became a Special Grade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:34.320
spirit called a Finger Bearer specifically&nbsp;
because it consumed one of Sukuna’s fingers.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.000
Instead of Yuji, Megumi, and Nobara’s&nbsp;
only options being to run or die,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:45.400
this time Itadori would have the power to fight.&nbsp;
Now in the real show, Sukuna made short work of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:51.120
this powerful cursed spirit - but in exchange&nbsp;
Yuji lost control of his body and Sukuna was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:56.080
able to take him hostage: AKA ripping out&nbsp;
his heart and threatening to kill him, only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.080 --> 00:05:01.880
offering to use his reversed curse technique to&nbsp;
heal him if he’ll make a Binding Vow - This vow,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:06.960
unbeknownst to Yuji since he literally forgot&nbsp;
about it due to the conditions of the bargain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:10.560
would have terrible, terrible,&nbsp;
TERRIBLE consequences down the line.

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.520
However, if Yuji could use Sukuna’s strength&nbsp;
without the downsides, he’d eliminate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.880
cursed spirit no problem. Sukuna showed&nbsp;
this Cursed Womb his domain expansion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.880
but since Yuji wouldn’t even know what&nbsp;
this was yet, he’d just put the Cursed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.920
Spirit through the Slap-Chop and cut it into a&nbsp;
million cursed pieces. Then the gang would all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:34.440
be free to grab a bowl of ramen afterward.&nbsp;
Of course, that’s not the only thing Yuji&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.720
gets to chow down on - he’d also be free to&nbsp;
chomp on yet another Sukuna finger that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:46.200
housed inside the Cursed Womb. This would bring&nbsp;
Yuji to a power level of exactly three fingers.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:52.360
It’s around this time that Jogo&nbsp;
would try to kill Gojo, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:57.840
this time Yuji wouldn’t be in secret training&nbsp;
since he didn’t fake die. I’m going to say that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.840 --> 00:06:03.480
Gojo would still have him do his Netflix Binge&nbsp;
Watch training program to try and get a hang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:08.720
on cursed energy. As Yuji’s finger number&nbsp;
increases more and more, the risk of Sukuna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.320
gaining control would be higher and higher, so&nbsp;
having him complete his cursed energy training&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:19.160
would be especially important. After all, even&nbsp;
if Sukuna didn’t take control, somebody without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:26.000
experience trying to use his power might&nbsp;
cause untold destruction just by accident.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:31.280
Anyway, Mr. Volcano Head would want to have&nbsp;
a word with Gojo, foolishly thinking that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:37.000
was even remotely a match. By the way, I&nbsp;
really wish his name was just Mr. Volcano&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:43.040
Head - that way I wouldn’t keep getting Jogo&nbsp;
and Gojo mixed up in my script. Thanks, Gege.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:48.000
Just like in the main series, Gojo would&nbsp;
use this opportunity to teach Yuji about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:52.120
the wonderful world of Domain&nbsp;
Expansion. This time, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:56.720
after seeing Gojo’s Unlimited Void&nbsp;
in action, Yuji would say “ooh, ooh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:03.000
ooh - let me try!” and whip out a Malevolent&nbsp;
Shrine. Or as Crunchyroll likes to call it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:09.640
a Malevolent Kitchen. However, Jogo isn’t getting&nbsp;
cooked just yet…we’ll save that for Shibuya.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:15.640
Outclassed by not one, but two Jujutsu Sorcerers,&nbsp;
Jogo would once again flee the scene with the help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:23.360
of his most flowery friend and decide that maybe&nbsp;
he needs Kenjaku’s help with Gojo after all.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.320
Onto Junpei! In the real timeline of Jujutsu&nbsp;
Kaisen, Yuji befriends a high school student&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:33.840
called Junpei. Unfortunately, Junpei had&nbsp;
made another friend recently: Mahito,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:39.960
the human curse - er, to be clear, that’s not&nbsp;
like a human/curse combo like Sukuna. No, Mahito&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:46.800
is a curse born from humanity’s fear of itself,&nbsp;
making him one of the scariest curses of all.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:50.360
Due to Junpei’s parents being divorced&nbsp;
and his constant bullying at school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:55.480
he’s adopted an extremely negative view of&nbsp;
humanity. Mahito takes advantage of this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:58.800
but Yuji genuinely tries&nbsp;
to become Junpei’s friend.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:03.680
However, this short arc culminates in&nbsp;
a huge battle at Junpei’s high school,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.680 --> 00:08:08.520
when Mahito uses his Idle Transfiguration&nbsp;
to turn Junpei into a monster who he can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:14.080
use against Yuji. According to Mahito,&nbsp;
there is no way to bring Junpei back.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:20.080
Yuji begs Sukuna for help. He knows Sukuna&nbsp;
can masterfully heal wounds - after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:24.480
he’d replaced Yuji’s entire heart with&nbsp;
Reverse Cursed Technique. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:28.760
in the real series Sukuna and Mahito&nbsp;
just laugh and mock Yuji in one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:35.680
most memorable panels from the whole series. Gege&nbsp;
Akutami sure knows how to draw a demented smile.

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:42.280
However, if Yuji could control Sukuna’s&nbsp;
powers, that would include his Reverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.280 --> 00:08:47.200
Cursed Technique. Using this power, he&nbsp;
could reverse Mahito’s ability. Mahito&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:51.560
states that it’s impossible to do, but&nbsp;
for all we know, Mahito just says this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:57.720
to harm Yuji more. Maybe with the power of&nbsp;
someone like Sukuna, it’s possible after all.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:03.560
Gege would have to take a cue from Eiichiro&nbsp;
Oda because Mahito would make a Shocked Enel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:10.360
face as Junpei was de-platypused. He’d&nbsp;
be so in shock, he’d barely see it coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:16.840
when Yuji pulled out the death by a thousand&nbsp;
cuts. Mahito can change the shape of souls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:22.320
but his soul would be in about a billion&nbsp;
pieces after Yuji was done with him.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:27.920
Yuji would be able to fight against him&nbsp;
with the full strength of Sukuna. AKA,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.000
Mahito’s getting cooked in the&nbsp;
Malevolent Kitchen. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:38.200
Yuji is no match for Mahito at this point in the&nbsp;
story, but Sukuna’s power outclasses him by miles.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:44.600
And Mahito being super dead is going to&nbsp;
really come into play later - you know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.600 --> 00:09:48.560
because of Shibuya. But for now,&nbsp;
Junpei and Yuji would celebrate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.840
Junpei realizing the errors of his ways&nbsp;
after Mahito took advantage of him and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:58.440
the two teens would go catch a movie&nbsp;
where absolutely no heads exploded.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:04.360
Up next, we get a Family Reunion where Itadori&nbsp;
gets to meet his siblings. Enter the Cursed Womb:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:10.160
Death Paintings. These guys are like the Cursed&nbsp;
Womb from earlier only wayyyyy worse. They were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:15.920
created by Kenjaku, the ultimate villain of JJK,&nbsp;
who was inhabiting the body of Noritoshi Kamo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:21.520
who gained the title of the most Evil Sorcerer&nbsp;
in HIstory. To create the Death Paintings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:27.800
he mixed the blood of cursed spirits and humans to&nbsp;
create creatures who were a hybrid of both. Aaaand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:36.640
since Kenjaku is also Yuji’s mom (long story),&nbsp;
this makes Eso, Kechizu, and Choso technically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:42.640
his brothers. Step brothers? Half brothers?&nbsp;
Curse brothers? Once again the team of Megumi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.640 --> 00:10:48.200
Kugisaki, and Yuji will destroy these guys and&nbsp;
Yuji will slurp up yet another delectable digit.

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:53.280
And now it’s the moment you’ve all&nbsp;
been waiting for! Happy Halloween&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:59.040
because in Jujutsu Kaisen time it’s October&nbsp;
31st…the night of the Shibuya Incident.

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:05.520
This is where the differences really&nbsp;
start coming along because Yuji has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:10.360
already destroyed Kenjaku’s plans.&nbsp;
Mahito was essential for helping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:14.800
keep Gojo busy and distracted so they could&nbsp;
trick him into getting caught by the Prison&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:20.960
Realm. Mahito also kills fan favorites&nbsp;
Nanami and maybe Nobara. Come on, Gege,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:25.880
would it kill you to just let us know what&nbsp;
happened to our favorite hammer girl already??

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:30.840
In this scenario, the Disaster Curses are&nbsp;
especially motivated to get rid of Gojo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:36.320
AND Yuji. They need Gojo clear so they can&nbsp;
fulfill their goal of taking out humanity and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:42.000
letting curses rule the world. The group&nbsp;
would still successfully capture Gojo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:49.560
but less thanks to the Disaster Curses and more&nbsp;
thanks to the Human Disaster: Kenjaku, or Pseudo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.560 --> 00:11:55.560
Geto as Gojo sees him. The World’s Strongest&nbsp;
Sorcerer would be caught in the Prison Realm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:00.120
leaving the rest of the fighters to deal with&nbsp;
three Special Grade Curses and their allies.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:04.880
Choso would still fight Yuji and slow him down&nbsp;
from being able to set Gojo free before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:11.120
Prison Realm was sealed, allowing Gojo to still be&nbsp;
captured. Choso would use his blood manipulation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:17.040
to fire off rounds at Yuji, but he’d dodge them&nbsp;
with ease. Just before Yuji uses his Sukuna powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:25.480
to absolutely chop up Choso, they’ll realize that&nbsp;
they are brothers. Yuji will be confused, but glad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:31.080
to accept another ally on their side as the two&nbsp;
go to face down the remaining Disaster Curses.

00:12:31.080 --> 00:12:35.480
During this arc, Mimiko and Nanako would&nbsp;
still feed Yuji a finger. These two girls&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:40.120
were followers of Suguru Geto prior to his&nbsp;
death, and therefore wanted to offer a finger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.120 --> 00:12:45.840
as an offering to Sukuna so that they could ask&nbsp;
him to kill Kenjaku for them since he had taken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:52.600
over their old master’s body. In the actual story&nbsp;
Sukuna kills them, perceiving them giving him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:57.560
an order as an unforgivable offense. However,&nbsp;
Yuji will be more than happy to use the finger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:03.320
boost to go after Kenjaku, especially since&nbsp;
Kenjaku just imprisoned his own master. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:03.320 --> 00:13:09.960
ever-polite Yuji would bow deeply after the gift&nbsp;
of another finger and go off to kill Kenjaku.

00:13:09.960 --> 00:13:16.480
However, Jogo would absolutely not give Yuji the&nbsp;
ten fingers he’d been hoarding. Since the King&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:21.360
of Curses was essentially being held hostage&nbsp;
by Yuji Itadori in this alternate timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:26.440
he’d want those fingers as far away&nbsp;
from Yuji as he could get them.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:32.280
Instead, in our timeline, it would come down to&nbsp;
an all out battle between the Disaster Curses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:36.400
Kenjaku, and Yuji’s Five Finger&nbsp;
Death Punch. However, Yuji would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.400 --> 00:13:40.160
have the backing of the other Jujutsu&nbsp;
Sorcerers. Of course, Hanami the nature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:40.160 --> 00:13:45.200
curse was already exorcised by Gojo before&nbsp;
he was trapped in the prison realm. Dagon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:49.680
the water-based curse would still be a problem,&nbsp;
but just like he does in the normal series the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:55.080
recently resurrected Toji Fushiguro would&nbsp;
be there to help beat the curse to a pulp.

00:13:55.080 --> 00:14:02.520
Jogo would be the biggest problem of the three.&nbsp;
Fifteen Finger Sukuna made short work of him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:08.120
but this time Yuji would only have five fingers&nbsp;
worth of strength. Therefore, he wouldn’t be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:13.840
able to absolutely flex on Mr. Volcano Head&nbsp;
with his own fire-based attack. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:21.120
Yuji would use his normal strategy of dicing&nbsp;
and slicing to turn Jogo into minced meat.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:27.160
All that’s left is Kenjaku, but after seeing&nbsp;
everything that had just gone down…well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:32.400
let’s just say Kenjaku is smart enough to read&nbsp;
the room and know when to dip. Getting up close&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.400 --> 00:14:37.880
and personal with the combat isn’t Kenjaku’s&nbsp;
usual style. The dude can absolutely fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:45.520
but he’s not trying to take on all of Jujutsu&nbsp;
High plus a Sukuna Strengthened Yuji. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:45.520 --> 00:14:51.160
he’s cunning and manipulative - he likes to&nbsp;
make plans and have others enact them for him.

00:14:52.920 --> 00:14:57.960
Since he’d lost Mahito, his biggest strategy&nbsp;
for enacting the Culling Game by stealing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:04.120
his ability was already gone, too. Therefore,&nbsp;
having succeeded in his goal of Sealing Gojo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:08.080
he’d retreat to gather new allies&nbsp;
and fight another day. Sadly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.280
this means he wouldn’t get to reunite&nbsp;
with his beloved son Yuji just yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.280 --> 00:15:17.760
but it would only be a matter of time before&nbsp;
he would get things to go his way once again.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:22.080
Of course, if Yuji did have control of&nbsp;
Sukuna’s power, the show wouldn’t be nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:27.520
as interesting unless they gave Yuji an enemy&nbsp;
who was truly on his level. If Sukuna’s power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:34.800
was on the side of good, what character could&nbsp;
possibly rival him? Gojo Satoru. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:40.480
he’s on our side, but if his backstory&nbsp;
